# rm Command (Remove)

`rm` is used to delete (remove) files and directories.

⚠️ Warning: Deleted files usually cannot be recovered.

---

## Remove a File

```bash
rm file.txt


| Command | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| `rm file.txt` | remove (delete) a file |
| `rm file1.txt file2.txt` | remove multiple files |
| `rm -i file.txt` | ask before deleting |
| `rm -r foldername` | remove directory and its contents |
| `rm -f file.txt` | force delete (no confirmation) |
| `rm -rf foldername` | force delete folder and everything inside (dangerous) |
